body:
The use of `require_once` prevents the routes from being loaded again after the Container has been recreated (refreshed) during testing. This causes the second test in this example to return a `404` and fail:

```php
<?php

class ExampleTest extends TestCase
{
    public function testFoo(): void
    {
        $this->get('/')->assertOk()->assertSee('Hyperf');
    }
    
    public function testBar(): void
    {
        $this->get('/')->assertOk()->assertSee('Hyperf');
    }
}
```

This PR fixes this by using `require` instead of `require_once` when loading the route file.

